  "rationale": "With no defences the attack succeeds, so at least one control is needed. Deploying mfa:admin alone is enough. Every exfiltrate technique needs admin_db, admin_fileserver or admin_backup. Each of those needs a foothold from an auth_* technique that requires stolen_dbadmin. stolen_dbadmin comes only from dump_dbadmin_dc or dump_dbadmin_adfs, which need admin_dc or admin_adfs. Those in turn need foothold_dc or foothold_adfs, which come only from auth_dc or auth_adfs, and both require NOT mfa_admin. So mfa:admin breaks every path to exfiltration."
